  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For an array AAA of length NNN, we define f(A)f(A)f(A) to be the smallest non-negative integer KKK such that AAA can be sorted in ascending order by using the following operation several (possibly, zero) times:\n\n\nChoose an index iii (1≤i&lt;N1 \\le i \\lt N1≤i&lt;N) such that Ai⊕Ai+1≤KA_i \\oplus A_{i+1} \\le KAi​⊕Ai+1​≤K.\nThen, swap AiA_iAi​ with Ai+1A_{i+1}Ai+1​.\nHere, ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise XOR operation.\n\nYou're given two integers NNN and KKK.\n\nFind any array AAA of length NNN satisfying the following properties:\n\n\n1≤Ai≤N1 \\le A_i \\le N1≤Ai​≤N for each 1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N, and\nAi≠AjA_i \\ne A_jAi​=Aj​ for 1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\le i \\lt j \\le N1≤i&lt;j≤N, and\nf(A)=Kf(A) = Kf(A)=K.\nIf there are multiple possible solutions, you may find any of them.\n\nIf no solution exists, print −1-1−1.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of a single line of input, containing two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the length of the array AAA and the required value of f(A)f(A)f(A), respectively.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case,\n\n\n\nIf no solution exists, print the single integer −1-1−1 on a new line.\nOtherwise, output NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ - the solution you found.\n\nIf there are multiple possible solutions, you may find any of them.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤K&lt;2N0 \\le K \\lt 2N0≤K&lt;2N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
